  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 124 PM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nThe holiday weekend started off on the warm, humid and for some \nstormy side. However, the pesky upper ridge aiding in this pattern \nwill retrograde somewhat and allow a brief return to more seasonable \ntemperatures (around 80 in the afternoon and 50s at night) through \nthe remainder of the extended weekend. Thereafter, the ridge tries \nto edge back NE Tuesday allowing slightly warmer and more humid \nconditions to return (still dry). A trough scoots across the \nnorthern US mid week, flattening out the ridge and allowing a weak \nboundary to linger in the area with some low end chances for showers \nand storms mainly Wed night into Thursday. \n\nAdditional waves pass north of the area, helping to limit the ridge \nfrom building back in (dangerous heat and humidity remains south of \nthe area) with possibly some chances for showers and storms with \neach wave into next weekend.",
